title: "Alberta Framework"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lawson
    given-names: Keith
  - name: "elizaOS research contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lalalune/alberta"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.27.0"
date-released: "2026-07-31"
keywords:
  - continual learning
  - meta-learning
  - reinforcement learning
  - adaptive step-sizes
  - JAX
  - IDBD
  - Autostep
  - Alberta Plan
abstract: >-
  A JAX-based research framework for investigating the Alberta Plan for
  continual AI. Focuses on adaptive step-size algorithms (IDBD, Autostep,
  SwiftTD), streaming nonlinear function approximation, GVF/Horde prediction,
  average-reward control, feature discovery and retention, and fail-closed
  evidence tooling for non-stationary supervised and reinforcement learning
  problems, with scan-based learning loops, online normalization, and
  publication-quality analysis tools.
